  "description": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=5ed02d2a7d0c250c236c34d9\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"5ed02d2a7d0c250c236c34d9\" data-account-id=\"5ed02d2a7d0c250c236c34d9\" accountid=\"5ed02d2a7d0c250c236c34d9\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Bethany Seeger</a> encountered an issue which results in the GET response for a versioned resource having an invalid ldp:contains statement.   </p>\n\n<p>If you have resource /a/ which contains resource /a/b/, then create a version of /a/b/, then PATCH /a/b/ to add a property to it, and then create a version of /a/, when you view the version of /a/ it ldp:contains something like /a/b/fcr:versions/vb instead of the expected /a/fcr:versions/va/b/.</p>\n\n<p>The issue can be replicated in 4.7.4 with the following curl commands:</p>\n\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\"></pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>curl -XPOST <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/</a> -H \"Slug: a\"<br/>\ncurl -XPOST <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/a\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/a</a> -H \"Slug: b\"<br/>\ncurl -XPOST <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/a/b/fcr:versions\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/a/b/fcr:versions</a> -H \"Slug: vb\"<br/>\ncurl -XPATCH <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/a/b\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/a/b</a> -d \"delete {} insert </p>\n{ &lt;&gt; &lt;http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title&gt; 'b title' }\n<p> where {} \" -H \"Content-Type: application/sparql-update\"<br/>\ncurl -XPOST <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/a/fcr:versions\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/a/fcr:versions</a> -H \"Slug: va\"<br/>\ncurl <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/a/fcr:versions/va\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/a/fcr:versions/va</a></p>\n<ol>\n\t<li>incorrectly includes \"ldp:contains &lt;<a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/a/b/fcr:versions/vb\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/a/b/fcr:versions/vb</a>&gt;\"</li>\n\t<li>Should have included \"ldp:contains &lt;<a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/a/fcr:versions/va/b\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/a/fcr:versions/va/b</a>&gt;\"</li>\n\t<li>Retrieve the resource referenced in va<br/>\ncurl <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/a/b/fcr:versions/vb\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/a/b/fcr:versions/vb</a></li>\n\t<li>when the snapshot of /a/ was created, /b/ had a dc:title, but the resource included in the snapshot does not have a dc:title because it is referencing the wrong version\n{/code}</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p>The incorrect ldp:contains issue actually occurs without the PATCH request, but including makes it clearer that va is referencing the wrong state of b.  This could effectively result inconsistent results or data loss when exporting versioned resources.</p>",
